course: dictionary
lesson: 6972
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word panel is a good example. «Solar panels make power only when the sun shines» is about a flat sheet that catches light, not a group of people.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. If it talks about a machine, a button or a switch, panel probably means a board with controls. If it talks about a contest, judges or choosing a winner, panel probably means a small group of people.
explain: In a comic, a panel is one box of the picture story. Read the clues around the word, then try each meaning in the sentence and pick the one that fits.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so check the context before you decide.
fact: A panel can be a flat piece of wood, glass, metal or other material that forms part of a door, wall or surface, like a «fence panel».
fact: A panel can be a board with switches, buttons or controls on it, like a «control panel».
fact: A panel can be a small group of people chosen to give their opinion or judge something, like a «panel of judges».
fact: In a comic strip, a panel is one picture box that helps tell the story in order.
exercise: «Solar panels make power only when the sun shines.» In this sentence, what is a solar panel? | A small group of people | A piece of cloth | *A flat piece that turns sunlight into electricity | A picture box in a comic
exercise: A contest needs a «panel of judges» to choose the winners. What does panel mean here? | A board of switches | *A small group of people chosen to judge | A flat piece of wood in a door | One box in a comic strip
exercise: Each panel of a comic strip shows one moment of the story. What is one panel? | A wall of a house | A control board for a machine | A group of judges | *One picture box in the story
test: The worker pressed a button on the «control panel» to stop the machine. What does panel mean? | A flat piece of wood in a fence | A picture box in a comic | A small group of people | *A board with switches, buttons or controls
test: «The fence panel blew down in the storm.» What is a fence panel? | *A flat piece of wood that is part of a fence | A type of rain | A picture box in a comic | A group of people who judge the fence
exam: «Each panel of the comic showed the hero getting closer to the villain.» What does panel mean? | A piece of metal on a door | A board with switches | A small group of people who give opinions | *One picture box in a comic strip
